{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5085",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with GI-ME-N, as it is a target of multiple pathways that ultimately lead to GI-ME-N. The first pathway connects Mollicellin N to A704, which is then targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and finally, palmarumycin CP18 targets GI-ME-N. In another pathway, Mollicellin N directly targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is subsequently targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets GI-ME-N. These two distinct pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence GI-ME-N. The integration of these evidence points implies that Mollicellin N may exert its effects on GI-ME-N through multiple, possibly overlapping, biological processes. The shared target of GI-ME-N in both pathways highlights the potential for a central role in the biological response to Mollicellin N.",
